Z||000007||MoneypitGT||06-28-2001||01:31 AM||||You can build them up to what ever you want, but you have to pay to play. You can even get titanium rods and valve springs for it, big $$. Best place I have found is <A HREF="http://www.mantapart.com," TARGET=_blank>www.mantapart.com,</A>  prices aren't the greatest but they have a lot of stuff. There is a Beretta that dynoed at 408hp supposedly and then threw a rod through the front and the back of the block. factory rods none the less. I guess someone learned a lesson.<BR>  Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||14
